# Placeholder

This directory will hold the 10 deliberately broken Playwright tests.

To be filled in during Episode 2 production (May 9-12, 2026):

1. `01-race-condition.spec.ts` — asserts on data before async fetch resolves
2. `02-dynamic-locator.spec.ts` — uses an ID that changes each render
3. `03-network-jitter.spec.ts` — assumes API response under 100ms
4. `04-time-based.spec.ts` — `Date.now()` comparison fails near midnight
5. `05-hover-focus.spec.ts` — hover state lost when DOM re-renders
6. `06-modal-timing.spec.ts` — clicks the modal trigger before listener attaches
7. `07-animation.spec.ts` — asserts on element position mid-CSS-transition
8. `08-viewport.spec.ts` — element only visible at certain widths
9. `09-iframe.spec.ts` — third-party iframe loads on its own timeline
10. `10-auth-flake.spec.ts` — session token expires mid-test

Each test should be ~15-25 lines, use realistic patterns (not contrived), and fail consistently when run.

Ask Claude to generate these using the prompt:
*"Generate 10 Playwright .spec.ts files, one per category above. Each should be a realistic test that fails because of that specific flakiness pattern — not because of contrived breakage. Tests should hit `http://localhost:3000` (the dashboard.html I'm about to build)."*
